---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import NextBand from '../components/NextBand.astro';
import { SITE, hasContactForm } from '../consts';

// Revised 11 October 2026: names the PDPL and the supervisory authority,
// describes the contact form's processor when the form is live, and no longer
// asserts a hosting region for a system this website does not contain.
const updated = '11 October 2026';
const formLive = hasContactForm();
---

<Base
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How NUMARATECH handles personal data collected through this website and in the course of providing its services."
>
  <PageHero
    kicker="Legal / Privacy"
    title="What we collect, and why."
    lead="This notice covers personal data that NUMARATECH handles through this website. Data we process on behalf of a client under a services agreement is governed by that agreement, not by this notice."
    stats={[
      { label: 'Last updated', value: updated },
      { label: 'Controller', value: SITE.legalName },
      { label: 'Contact', value: SITE.email },
      { label: 'Trackers', value: 'none' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="nt-section">
    <div class="nt-prose">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>

      <p>There are two ways personal data reaches us from this site.</p>

      <h3>Information you send us</h3>
      {
        formLive ? (
          <p>
            If you write to us through the enquiry form, email us or telephone
            us, we receive what you chose to provide — typically your name,
            email address, company, and the substance of your enquiry. The form
            is delivered by Web3Forms, a form-handling service that passes your
            message to our mailbox and does not use it for anything else. We
            use what you send to answer you and to keep a record of the
            conversation.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            This site has no contact form. If you email or telephone us, we
            receive what you chose to provide — typically your name, email
            address, company, and the substance of your enquiry. We use it to
            answer you and to keep a record of the conversation.
          </p>
        )
      }

      <h3>Technical information</h3>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider records standard request information such as IP
        address, user agent and the page requested. This is used to serve the
        site, protect it from abuse, and understand aggregate traffic. We do not
        combine it with anything that identifies you personally.
      </p>

      <h3>What we deliberately do not collect</h3>
      <p>
        This site sets no advertising or tracking cookies and loads no
        third-party analytics, fonts or scripts. Fonts are served from our own
        domain. The Corporate Tax estimator runs entirely in your browser — the
        figures you enter are never transmitted to us, are not stored, and are
        gone when you close the tab.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we are allowed to hold it</h2>

      <p>
        We process personal data on the bases the PDPL permits — principally
        your consent, the performance of a contract with you, and our
        legitimate interests in responding to enquiries and running the
        practice. Where you contact us, we rely on your consent and on that
        legitimate interest. Where we keep records of a commercial
        relationship, we rely on legitimate interest and on legal obligations
        that require us to retain certain records. Where we rely on consent you
        may withdraw it at any time, and we will stop unless another basis
        applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>

      <p>
        We use a small number of service providers to operate the business, and
        they see only what their function requires:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting and content delivery.</strong> Serves this site and
          processes request logs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email mailbox.</strong> Carries and stores the messages you
          send us.
        </li>
        {
          formLive && (
            <li>
              <strong>Form delivery.</strong> Web3Forms receives what you type
              into the enquiry form and forwards it to our mailbox.
            </li>
          )
        }
      </ul>

      <p>
        We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it for anyone else's
        marketing. We will disclose data where we are legally required to, and
        will tell you if that happens unless we are prohibited from doing so.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is held</h2>

      <p>
        This website holds no client data. It is a static site with no database
        and no server-side processing, and the Corporate Tax estimator runs
        entirely in your browser.
      </p>

      <p>
        Data you send us is held in our mailbox and may be processed outside
        the United Arab Emirates by the providers above; where that happens we
        rely on their contractual data protection commitments. Where we process
        client data under a signed services agreement, the hosting location is
        set out in that agreement — ask us before you sign if the location
        matters to you, and we will confirm it in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>

      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become a commercial relationship are deleted
        within 24 months. Records relating to a client relationship are retained
        for the period required by applicable law and for as long as needed to
        deal with any question arising from the engagement, then deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>

      <p>
        This notice is written to meet UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on
        the Protection of Personal Data (the PDPL) and its implementing
        decisions. Where the PDPL gives you a right that this notice does not
        mention, you still have it.
      </p>

      <p>
        You may ask us to give you a copy of the personal data we hold about
        you, correct it if it is wrong, delete it where we have no continuing
        basis to keep it, or stop using it for a particular purpose. Data
        protection questions and requests are handled by the practice owner.
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, marked
        "Data protection", and we will respond within 30 days.
      </p>

      <p>
        If we cannot resolve a concern to your satisfaction, you may complain
        to the UAE Data Office, the federal authority responsible for personal
        data protection in the United Arab Emirates. If you are outside the
        UAE, you may also complain to the data protection authority where you
        live.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>

      <p>
        Access to data is limited to people who need it for their work, secured
        with multi-factor authentication, and logged. Client environments are
        separated per entity. No system is perfect; if we become aware of a
        breach affecting your data we will tell you promptly and tell you what
        we know.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>

      <p>
        We will update this page when our practices change, and revise the date
        above. Material changes affecting existing clients will be communicated
        directly rather than only posted here.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Questions about this notice or about how we handle your data:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, or write to us at
        {' '}{SITE.address.line1}, {SITE.address.city},
        {' '}{SITE.address.country}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <NextBand
    title="Questions about your data?"
    body="Write to us and we will answer within 30 days — including a copy of what we hold, or its deletion where we have no continuing basis to keep it."
    cta="Email us"
    href="/contact/"
  />
</Base>
